hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2895","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, narrated to us Shu'bah, who said: I heard Qatadah narrating, from Anas ibn Malik (RA), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to sacrifice two horned rams that were white with black markings. He would recite the name of Allah and say \Allahu Akbar\"" (Allah is the Greatest)"," and I saw him slaughtering them with his own hand"," placing his foot on their sides.\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
"2896","Narrated to us by Ali bin Khushram, who said: Isa bin Yunus informed us, on the authority of Shu'bah, on the authority of Qatadah, who said: I heard Anas bin Malik (RA) saying: I asked him, \Did you hear this yourself?\"" He replied"," \""Yes.\"" He said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would sacrifice an animal similar to this.\"""""
